== HttpSAMLClient ==

The <code>HttpSAMLClient</code> is an alternative SAML client implementation for the '''SimpleSAMLphp''' MediaWiki extension. Instead of loading SimpleSAMLphp directly into the MediaWiki PHP process (shared autoloader), it communicates with a standalone SimpleSAMLphp installation over HTTP.

This avoids class autoloader and dependency collisions described in:
* [https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T394009 T394009]
* [https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T383351 T383351]

=== Architecture overview ===

<pre>
┌────────────────────┐         HTTP (internal)        ┌─────────────────────────┐
│   MediaWiki        │  ─────────────────────────────▶│  SimpleSAMLphp          │
│   (HttpSAMLClient) │                                │  public/api/session.php │
└────────────────────┘                                └─────────────────────────┘
</pre>

The <code>HttpSAMLClient</code> forwards the user's SimpleSAMLphp session cookies and an API token to a dedicated endpoint (<code>session.php</code>) on the SimpleSAMLphp installation. This endpoint returns session status, login URLs, and logout URLs as JSON.

=== Configuration ===

==== LocalSettings.php ====


Add the following configuration to your <code>LocalSettings.php</code> file:

<syntaxhighlight lang="php">
$GLOBALS['wgPluggableAuth_Config']['Log in with SAML'] = [
    'plugin' => 'SimpleSAMLphp',
    'data' => [
        'authSourceId' => 'default-sp',
        'usernameAttribute' => 'username',
        'realNameAttribute' => 'name',
        'emailAttribute' => 'email'
    ],
];

// Switch to the HTTP-based SAML client
$GLOBALS['SimpleSAMLphp_SAMLClient'] = 'http-client';

// Configure the HTTP client connection
$GLOBALS['SimpleSAMLphp_HTTPClientConfig'] = [
    'baseUrl' => 'http://localhost/saml/',
    'sessionIdCookieName' => 'SimpleSAMLSessionID',
    'authTokenCookieName' => 'SimpleSAMLAuthToken',
    'sessionAPItoken' => 'your-shared-secret-token'
];
</syntaxhighlight>

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Parameter !! Description
|-
| <code>SimpleSAMLphp_SAMLClient</code> || Set to <code>'http-client'</code> to use the HTTP-based client instead of the default shared-autoloader client.
|-
| <code>baseUrl</code> || Base URL of the SimpleSAMLphp <code>public/</code> directory as accessible from MediaWiki (server-to-server).
|-
| <code>sessionIdCookieName</code> || Name of the SimpleSAMLphp session ID cookie (must match <code>session.cookie.name</code> in SimpleSAMLphp's <code>config.php</code>).
|-
| <code>authTokenCookieName</code> || Name of the SimpleSAMLphp auth token cookie (must match <code>session.authtoken.cookiename</code> in SimpleSAMLphp's <code>config.php</code>).
|-
| <code>sessionAPItoken</code> || A shared secret used to authenticate API calls from MediaWiki to the session endpoint (must match <code>mediawiki.sessionapi.token</code> in SimpleSAMLphp's <code>config.php</code>).
|}

==== SimpleSAMLphp config.php ====

In your SimpleSAMLphp <code>config/config.php</code>, add the following settings to protect the session API endpoint:

<syntaxhighlight lang="php">
'mediawiki.sessionapi.token' => 'your-shared-secret-token',
'mediawiki.sessionapi.allowedcallers' => '127.16.0.12/16',
</syntaxhighlight>

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Parameter !! Description
|-
| <code>mediawiki.sessionapi.token</code> || Must match the <code>sessionAPItoken</code> value configured in MediaWiki. Must not be empty.
|-
| <code>mediawiki.sessionapi.allowedcallers</code> || Comma-separated list of CIDR ranges allowed to call the API (e.g. <code>172.16.0.0/12, 127.0.0.1/32</code>). HINT: Calls from <code>localhost</code> are always allowed.
|}

=== Installing the session.php endpoint ===

The file <code>_simplesamlphp/public/api/session.php</code> (shipped with this extension) must be placed into the SimpleSAMLphp installation at:

<pre>
<simplesamlphp-root>/public/api/session.php
</pre>

==== Manual installation ====

Copy the file from the extension source:

<syntaxhighlight lang="bash">
cp extensions/SimpleSAMLphp/_simplesamlphp/public/api/session.php \
   /path/to/simplesamlphp/public/api/session.php
</syntaxhighlight>

=== Security ===

The <code>session.php</code> endpoint is protected by two mechanisms:

# '''Shared token''' — A secret token sent via the <code>X-SIMPLESAMLPHP-SESSION-API-TOKEN</code> HTTP header.
# '''IP allowlisting''' — Only requests from configured CIDR ranges (via <code>mediawiki.sessionapi.allowedcallers</code>) are accepted.

Both checks must pass for a request to be processed. Ensure:
* The token is kept secret and not committed to version control. Use environment variables / secrets.
* The allowed CIDR range is as restrictive as possible (ideally only the MediaWiki container/server IP).

=== How it works ===

# User visits MediaWiki and triggers SAML authentication.
# <code>HttpSAMLClient</code> calls SimpleSAMLphp's <code>session.php?action=status</code>, forwarding the user's SSP session cookies.
# If not authenticated, it calls <code>session.php?action=login-url&returnTo=...</code> and redirects the user to the IdP login.
# After IdP authentication, the user returns to MediaWiki with valid SSP session cookies.
# <code>HttpSAMLClient</code> retrieves user attributes via <code>session.php?action=status</code>.
# For logout, it calls <code>session.php?action=logout-url&returnTo=...</code> and redirects the user.

=== Available API actions ===

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Action !! Description !! Response fields
|-
| <code>status</code> || Check authentication state and retrieve attributes || <code>authenticated</code> (bool), <code>attributes</code> (object)
|-
| <code>login-url</code> || Get the IdP login URL || <code>loginUrl</code> (string)
|-
| <code>logout-url</code> || Get the logout URL || <code>logoutUrl</code> (string)
|}

All requests accept the query parameters <code>authSourceId</code> (default: <code>default-sp</code>) and <code>returnTo</code> (for login/logout URL generation).
